@@ -586,0 +587,14
+  Debug start (`port/src/debug_start.cpp`): `town:<0-4>` is `edit:<0-4>`
+  (Norune, Matataki, Queens, Muska Racka, Yellow Drops); `dungeon:<n>:<floor>`
+  enters that floor (1 up, to 15, 17, 18, 18, 15, 25 and 100) directly through
+  retail's requested-floor entry (`InitDunEnterMenu`) and marks it reached;
+  `pick` shows a list of the towns and dungeons in the developer menu's place:
+  Up/Down a row, Left/Right a floor (L1/R1 by ten), Cross starts there, Circle
+  goes back where the list was opened (at boot, on to the title). Pad 1's
+  L3+R3 opens the same list at any time, in every build and launcher; linked,
+  it reads the lockstep's pads, so both copies open it on the same tick and
+  travel together. A floor start gives the party the members the story has by
+  that dungeon (each with its starting weapon) and marks the first-visit
+  scenes seen (game flag 103, Divine Beast Cave). A debug start turns
+  `DebugMode` on; a join's resync then sends both copies straight back onto
+  the host's floor rather than to its floor menu.
@@ -772,0 +787,5
+- The attract movie's loading screen shows the SCE and Level-5 logos (about
+  800 ticks). Start or Cross on either controller, or their keyboard bindings
+  (Enter, Space), ends them with a short fade; while `game.netplay` is set only
+  a controller does (`port/src/coop/coop_boot.hpp`). The logos come before the
+  first frame, so an input script's frame-0 line is what is held through them.
